# tools/c/control_perturbation_witness.rish -- does a guard's ANSWER move when its own control
# goes away?
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. Its sibling `tools/c/control_in_population_witness.rish` counts MEMBERSHIP: a
# guard's enumerated population holds a tracked file of the guard's own family. That reading names
# its own upper bound and says why -- a scan may enumerate broadly and filter narrowly, so
# membership is no proof the scan READS the file. It also names a whole class it cannot reach at
# all: `no_git_population`, a scan spelling no `git ls-files`, counted apart and reported as
# GENUINELY UNMEASURED rather than clear, since a `find` rooted at the repository root or under
# `tools/` reaches a control just as well.
#
# WHY THAT CLASS CANNOT BE WIDENED INTO, measured `20260916` over the 198 tracked scans naming no
# `git ls-files`. Every `find` root in the reachable subset is a loop variable or a per-scan
# directory variable -- `$room`, `$DIR`, `$DESK_DIR`, `$root_dir` -- and the sibling's admit rule
# refuses a variable on purpose, because evaluating one is evaluating whatever a scan happens to
# hold. Widening the rule would not resolve those roots; it would only run them blind. Only
# RUNNING the scan reaches this class, which is what this rung does.
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED, on metal. Each candidate is run twice in a detached worktree at HEAD: once
# whole, once with its family INSTRUMENT absent from the index AND from the working tree. The two
# outputs are compared. `unmoved` is byte-identical. `moved` differs in some reading with every
# `verdict=` line still agreeing. `verdict_flipped` differs in a verdict, which is a guard whose
# PASS is partly a statement about its own instrument rather than about the field.
#
# WHY BOTH HALVES OF THE PERTURBATION. A scan enumerating with `git ls-files` reads the index; a
# scan enumerating with `find` reads the filesystem. One perturbation answers for both populations
# or the reading is a statement about enumeration style rather than about the guard.
#
# A FAMILY INSTRUMENT IS RESOLVED BY ROLE RATHER THAN BY NAME, which is this rung's second lap.
# The first reading skipped three of its nine candidates for holding no tracked `_control.sh`, and
# that one word covered three different states. Two of the three carry a control by ROLE, under
# another name and in another room: `tools_py_ban_scan.sh` plants
# `context/fixtures/tools_py_ban_tree/tools/planted.py` and hands its selftest a scan-root
# override, and `copy_sameness_scan.sh` plants `context/fixtures/copy_sameness_drift/
# tally_copy_drifted.rye` under a basename its own `find` excludes. The third,
# `living_docs_lint_scan.sh`, holds a roster and a keeps allowlist, which it READS as input rather
# than planting to be found -- and that one is genuinely unmeasurable. The ROOM decides, because
# `context/fixtures/` held 12 tracked files on `20260916` and every one is a planted fixture, while
# `tools/fixtures/` holds the instruments that read them.
#
# THE READING, `20260916`, over the same nine candidates: 5 probed, 4 unmoved, 1 moved, 0 verdict
# flipped, 1 plant probed, 1 skipped for holding no family instrument at all, and 3 refused for a
# cause this rung names. The widening moved two of the three skips: one into a real reading
# (`copy_sameness`, unmoved -- its plant stands outside its own population by basename) and one
# into the named refusal, since `tools_py_ban_scan.sh` carries the root-finder below. Set beside
# the sibling's 37 enumerable scans, which came back 24 unmoved, 13 moved and 2 flipped, the class
# the census could not reach is the CLEANER of the two -- so the blind spot was a blind spot rather
# than a hiding place. Every figure here is FREE: run the scan.
#
# THE ONE MOVER IS THE HEALTHY SHAPE, which is worth more than a refusal would have been.
# `tools/fixtures/i/instrument_absence_scan.sh` moves `scans_read` by one and
# `blind_captures_in_fixture` from 9 to 0 -- and that second counter exists precisely to hold the
# nine sites standing inside its own control, counted apart from the field. Its control already
# proves the exemption in both directions by name. A guard that reads its own control and SAYS SO
# in a field of its own is the answer to the class, rather than an instance of it.
#
# THE REFUSAL THIS RUNG NAMES, and the wider fact behind it. 164 tracked shell scripts -- 74 of
# them `*_scan.sh` -- find the repository root by walking up to a directory `rishi/bin`. Nothing
# under `rishi/bin` is tracked: it holds the built binary. So a checkout of tracked bytes alone
# has no such directory, and every one of the 164 refuses with `no tree root within 8 steps`
# before reading a file. The probe classifies that refusal by name rather than reporting it blind,
# because a named cause can be repaired. The repair is one directory name -- `rishi/src` is
# tracked and, measured `20260916`, both `rishi/src/` and `tools/fixtures/` occur at the
# repository root and nowhere below it, so it is exactly as discriminating. The bootstrap is NOT
# circular: `tools/fixtures/r/rye_build.sh` carries no root-finder, so a fresh clone still builds
# `rishi` and every script then works. The cost is latent rather than live.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED AND NEVER GATED. A moved reading may be entirely correct, as the one mover here
# is. A gate would refuse the repaired shape beside the unrepaired one, and a gate that reds on a
# correct tree is a gate somebody turns off.
#
# ONE WRITER PER CHECKOUT (REDS %291) is the rule this rung most easily breaks: the pen is a second
# checkout of this repository. It is created under `mktemp -d`, outside the tree so no peer's
# `find .` walks it, and removed on every exit path. The first ad-hoc run of this probe was
# discarded on `20260916` for exactly that fault, when a hand entered the pen mid-probe.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. Whether a moved reading is a fault; that is judgment, and the classification
# is what tells a reader there is a judgment to make. A candidate holding no family instrument at
# all stays unread rather than clean -- there is nothing to take away. And an `unmoved` reading on
# a PLANT says the plant stands outside that guard's population; it says nothing about whether the
# guard would have been right to read it.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/c/control_perturbation_witness.rish

say "control-perturbation: Language EN -- membership is not reading; running the guard twice is."
say "control-perturbation: Style Gauge at Field -- every figure carries its denominator and its refusals."
say "control-perturbation: Lens TAME -- safety first: a guard's green may be partly about its own instrument."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/control_perturbation_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "control-perturbation: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "control-perturbation: the control must agree with itself"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "control-perturbation: every leg must stand, and a leg written tomorrow must be heard today"
assert control.out contains "leg candidates_hold_find_rooted ok" else "control-perturbation: a find-rooted scan is the class this instrument exists for"
assert control.out contains "leg candidates_read_past_git_enumerating ok" else "control-perturbation: a scan the sibling already measures is not this instrument's candidate"
assert control.out contains "leg candidates_read_past_the_probe_itself ok" else "control-perturbation: the probe must never probe itself"
assert control.out contains "leg unmoved_named ok" else "control-perturbation: the clear direction is asserted as hard as the refusal"
assert control.out contains "leg moved_named ok" else "control-perturbation: a guard counting its own control must be named"
assert control.out contains "leg verdict_flip_named ok" else "control-perturbation: a flipped verdict is the sharpest reading and earns its own class"
assert control.out contains "leg flip_is_not_counted_as_moved ok" else "control-perturbation: the two classes answer different questions and must move apart"
assert control.out contains "leg lonely_skipped ok" else "control-perturbation: a scan with no family instrument is unread, never clean"
assert control.out contains "leg plant_resolved_by_room ok" else "control-perturbation: a control by role, planted in the tree's own fixture room, must resolve"
assert control.out contains "leg plant_removal_moves_a_reader ok" else "control-perturbation: removing a plant must perturb a guard whose population reaches it"
assert control.out contains "leg control_preferred_over_plant ok" else "control-perturbation: a family holding both kinds loses the nearer instrument, so the reading is one thing"
assert control.out contains "leg plant_never_skipped ok" else "control-perturbation: a plant-bearing family must leave the unmeasurable class"
assert control.out contains "leg count_plants_probed ok" else "control-perturbation: the plant half of the population is counted apart from the control half"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_plant_branch_bites ok" else "control-perturbation: dropping the plant branch must return the plant-bearing families to the skip"
assert control.out contains "leg rootfinder_refusal_named ok" else "control-perturbation: a refusal whose cause is known must be named rather than reported blind"
assert control.out contains "leg other_refusal_stays_plain ok" else "control-perturbation: a cause the probe cannot name must stay a plain refusal"
assert control.out contains "leg restore_keeps_one_baseline ok" else "control-perturbation: every candidate must be measured against the same tree"
assert control.out contains "leg index_half_moves ok" else "control-perturbation: the index half of the perturbation must reach a git-enumerating scan"
assert control.out contains "leg live_control_survives ok" else "control-perturbation: the pen's own tree must be left as it was found"
assert control.out contains "leg no_worktree_leaked ok" else "control-perturbation: a worktree left behind is a second writer in someone's checkout"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_worktree_half_bites ok" else "control-perturbation: dropping the worktree half must blind the find population"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_index_half_bites ok" else "control-perturbation: dropping the index half must blind the git-ls-files population"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_restore_bites ok" else "control-perturbation: dropping the restore must show as two candidates disagreeing about one tree"
say "control GREEN -- 35 legs on real git repositories in a throwaway pen, four mutations bitten"

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/control_perturbation_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "control-perturbation: the probe must complete before it is believed"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=reported" else "control-perturbation: this reading reports and never gates"
assert scan.out contains "perturbation=family_instrument_absent_from_index_and_worktree" else "control-perturbation: what was taken away must be said out loud"
assert scan.out contains "skipped_no_instrument=" else "control-perturbation: a candidate with nothing to take away is counted apart, never proven clear"
assert scan.out contains "plants_probed=" else "control-perturbation: a control by role is counted apart from a control by name"
assert scan.out contains "refused=" else "control-perturbation: a candidate that would not run is counted rather than vanishing"
assert scan.out contains "refused_root_finder_needs_built_tree=" else "control-perturbation: the named refusal must be told apart from the unnamed one"
assert scan.out contains "verdict_flipped=" else "control-perturbation: the sharpest reading must be printed even when it reads zero"

say "control-perturbation GREEN -- the class the membership census could not reach is measured and is the cleaner of the two"
